From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Bump qs 6.14.1 -> 6.16.1 for CVE-2026-110816

Upstream: https://github.com/ljharb/qs/commit/a952e7519338ef0cfb25694a2988848f93333727

qs.stringify with arrayFormat: 'comma' throws TypeError: Cannot convert
object to primitive value when an array element cannot be coerced to a
string, such as an object with a non-callable own toString or a
null-prototype object. An unauthenticated request can make any code
path that re-serializes attacker-influenced data with qs.stringify and
arrayFormat: 'comma' throw synchronously; outside a framework error
boundary (e.g. an async Express 4 handler) the process exits. Fixed in
6.16.1.
Yarn cache regenerated and uploaded to lookaside.

